QE = {0: "Now the unification, arrived in due course, is discussed.", 1: "Since it was said the triad is to be worshipped together with the cakra-divisions: here, in this manner, is their unification.", 2: "Viśvā, her Mistress, Hāraudrī, Vīranetrī, Ambikā, and Gurvī, thus: the goddesses shown in the Siddhāvīra, in the six-spoked wheel.", 3: "Māheśī, Brāhmaṇī, Skāndī, Vaiṣṇavī, Aindrī, Yamātmikā, Cāmuṇḍā indeed, and Yogīśī — thus eight, or the Aghorī-group and the rest.", 4: "Joined with the twelve — the mothers of Fire, Nirṛti, Wind, and Īśa: Nandā, Bhadrā, Jayā, Kālī, Karālī, Vikṛtānanā.", 5: "Kroṣṭukī and Bhīmamudrā, Vāyuvegā, Hayānanā, Gambhīrā, and Ghoṣaṇī, thus: the rule in the twenty-four-spoked wheel.", 6: "Siddhi, Vṛddhi, Dyuti, Lakṣmī, Medhā, Kānti, Sudhā, Dhṛti, Dīpti, Puṣṭi, Mati, Kīrti, Susthiti, Sugati, Smṛti.", 7: "Suprabhā — sixteen in all, thus: the Śrīkaṇṭha-headed powers. Bali and Balinanda, Daśagrīva, Hara, Haya.", 8: "Mādhava in the six-spoked wheel; but in the twelve-spoked these are remembered: Dakṣa, Caṇḍa, Hara, Śauṇḍī, Pramatha, Bhīma and Manmatha.", 9: "Śakuni, Sumati, Nanda, Gopāla and Pitāmaha; Śrīkaṇṭha, Ananta, Sūkṣma, and Trimūrti, Śaṃbareśvara.", 10: "Arghīśa and Bhārabhūti, Sthiti, Sthāṇu, Hara, thus; Jhaṇṭi, Bhautika, Sadyoja, Anugraha, Krūra, Sainika.", 11: "Two-eight; whatever nectar, joined therewith: Pūrṇa, Ābha and their fluids, Ogha, Ūrmi, Syandana, Aṅga, and Vapus, Udgāra, Vaktraka.", 12: "Tanu, Secana, Mūrti, Īśa; Sarvāmṛtadhara, and the other; by feminine reading these powers are declared sixteen indeed.", 13: "Saṃvarta, Lakulī, Bhṛgu, Sita, Baka, Khaṅgī, Pinākī, Bhujaga, Bali, Kāla; Dvi and Chagalāṇḍa; Śikhī, Śoṇa, Meṣa, Mīna, Tridaṇḍī; with Āṣāḍhī.", 14: "Devīkānta and his half; Dāruka, Hali, Somanātha, Śarman; Jaya, Vijaya, Jayantā, Jita, Sujaya, Jaya, the Rudrakīrtana-bringers.", 15: "Increasing zeal for His form; and the Bala, Subala, Bhadra gift-bearers; its bearer and giver, and the Lord, joyous, equal, blessed of His form.", 16: "Desiring well-minded Śiva-giving; Durga, time called Bhadra, mind-following Kauśika, Kāla, Viśva, Suśivās and others likewise; Kopa.", 17: "On the ear-fire spoke these would be; by feminine reading these are śaktis. 'Juṃkāra' and 'Agnipatnī', thus, in the six-spoked, eunuch-excluded.", 18: "In the twelve-spoked, those along with them; in the sixteen-spoked, the vowels in order; ha in the twice-eight-spoked; from ya to the ha-end, but, in the trika.", 19: "On the thirty-two-spoked, with end, bindu on the head of all; thus many other cakra-divisions one should construct from this.", 20: "One alone is this consciousness-self, the essence of universe-awareness; śakti and her possessor thence — mother, mass of sound — are declared a pair.", 21: "But in the division of those two, in the fashioning of śakti and her possessor: the sound-mass and Mālinī, of agitation-nature, such a body.", 22: "Thus in the splitting of inner awareness, really the triad called Anuttara, Icchā, Unmeṣa — from which the universe is awareness.", 23: "But in union with Ānanda, Īśa, Ūrmi, that is declared the hexad; through semivowel-sibilant union that is declared the octad.", 24: "Then, in the absence of the four amṛta-vowels, it would be a dodecad; in union with them, called sixteen — thus until innumerability.", 25: "Since it clearly bears the universe from single-awareness-bearing on, bearing part-of-part awarenesses at the end.", 26: "Hence the fifty's oneness, vowel-manifest-variety, eight vargas, letter-division, eighty-one kalā-rise.", 27: "Thus shown before, from half-mora-bearing; for even vowel-half exists, of the svarita a half-mora.", 28: "From its beginning the udātta, that said by the pada-knower; thus this consciousness, of sacrificand-form-awareness-nature.", 29: "Unbroken from consciousness, this wheel-horizon of wheels; by lordship-and-veil division employ it manifoldly.", 30: "Parāparā, Parā, and the other: creation, maintenance, concealment; but the fourth, Mātṛsadbhāva-formed, is called repose.", 31: "And that clearly mouth-seated, hinted at each word; in the Fourth, repose is to be placed, moving in Mātṛsadbhāva.", 32: "So to him the universe shines, gone to identity with his own self; thus told is this unification of the scripture's matter, uttered by the guru."}


def main() -> None:
    spans = source_spans('tantraloka-a33')
    assert {int(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()} == {k: v for k, v in spans.items()}, 'TOKENS DRIFT'
    assert all(len(TOK[v]) == len(CM[v]) == len(GLOSS[v]) for v in TOK), 'ROW DRIFT'
    json.dump({str(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()}, open('tantraloka-a33/cm/spans-tal-a33.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    cm = {}
    for v in TOK:
        cm[str(v)] = [[CM[v][i][0], CM[v][i][1], CM[v][i][2]] for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]
    json.dump(cm, open('tantraloka-a33/cm/l0cm-v0-32.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    t1 = [{"verse_id": "tal-a33-v%02d" % v, "song": "tal-a33", "verse": v, "quick_english": QE[v], "quick_english_source": "manual", "tokens": [{"surface": TOK[v][i], "quick_gloss": GLOSS[v][i]} for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]} for v in sorted(TOK)]
    json.dump(t1, open('tantraloka-a33/working-t1-tal-a33.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    md = '# Tantraloka-a33 — T1\n*Source: GRETIL tantraloka (KSTS) via workcfg taloka. Span-exact vs source_spans. Machine-proposed, needs human review.*\n'
    for v in sorted(TOK):
        md += '\n\n## tal-a33-v%02d\n' % v
        md += ' '.join('[and]-%s (%s)' % (GLOSS[v][i], TOK[v][i]) for i in range(len(TOK[v]))) + ' // %d //\n' % v
    open('tantraloka-a33/T1-tal-a33.md', 'w').write(md)
    print('cm+t1 written, verses:', len(t1), 'tokens:', sum(len(x) for x in TOK.values()))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
